## Database Schema

### `packages` table

| Column | Type | Notes |
|--------|------|-------|
| `id` | bigIncrements | PK |
| `name_en` | string(255) | e.g. "2 Hours" |
| `name_ru` | string(255) | e.g. "2 Часа" |
| `name_it` | string(255) | e.g. "2 Ore" |
| `description_en` | text | English description |
| `description_ru` | text | Russian description |
| `description_it` | text | Italian description |
| `price` | decimal(8,2) | e.g. 150.00 |
| `currency` | string(3) | `'USD'`, `'EUR'`, or `'RUB'` — chosen by admin per package |
| `hours` | decimal(4,1) | e.g. 2.0, 4.0, 8.0 — for sorting/display |
| `is_active` | boolean | Default `true` |
| `is_featured` | boolean | Default `false` — the "Popular" badge |
| `sort_order` | unsignedInteger | Default `0` |
| `timestamps` | | created_at, updated_at |

### `bookings` table

| Column | Type | Notes |
|--------|------|-------|
| `id` | bigIncrements | PK |
| `package_id` | foreignId, nullable | FK → `packages.id`, set null on delete |
| `name` | string(255) | Customer name |
| `phone` | string(30) | Phone number (without country code) |
| `country_code` | string(5) | Country dial code with `+` prefix (e.g. `"+20"`, `"+7"`) — extracted from `intl-tel-input` |
| `email` | string(255), nullable | Optional email |
| `status` | enum | `'new'`, `'contacted'`, `'confirmed'`, `'completed'`, `'cancelled'` — default `'new'` |
| `notes` | text, nullable | Admin internal notes |
| `timestamps` | | created_at, updated_at |

> [!NOTE]
> `package_id` uses `nullOnDelete()` — if a package is deleted, the booking record stays but the package reference becomes null. This preserves order history.

