## intl-tel-input Integration

### CDN Assets (loaded in public layout or booking section)

```html
<!-- CSS -->
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/intl-tel-input@23.0.4/build/css/intlTelInput.css">

<!-- JS (before Alpine) -->
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/intl-tel-input@23.0.4/build/js/intlTelInput.min.js"></script>
```

### Alpine Integration in Booking Form

```js
x-data="{
    form: { name: '', phone: '', country_code: '+20', email: '', package_id: '' },
    iti: null,
    loading: false,
    errors: {},
    success: false,
    init() {
        this.$nextTick(() => {
            const input = this.$refs.phoneInput;
            this.iti = window.intlTelInput(input, {
                initialCountry: 'eg',
                preferredCountries: ['eg', 'sa', 'ae', 'kw', 'qa', 'bh', 'om', 'jo', 'lb'],
                separateDialCode: true,
                utilsScript: 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/intl-tel-input@23.0.4/build/js/utils.js',
            });
            input.addEventListener('countrychange', () => {
                const data = this.iti.getSelectedCountryData();
                this.form.country_code = '+' + data.dialCode;
            });
        });
    },
    async submit() { /* fetch POST, handle 200/422/429 */ }
}"
```

### Backend Storage

- `country_code`: stored with `+` prefix (e.g. `"+20"`) — extracted from `intl-tel-input`
- `phone`: the number part only (e.g. `"1234567890"`)
- Admin sees full number: `+20 1234567890`

